# Everything in here is environment-specific and stays local.
#
# An environment is a directory (prod/) holding what deploy.sh and
# set-context.sh read for it: <release>-values.yaml, kubeconfig.yaml and,
# optionally, manifests/. The kubeconfig is a cluster credential and a
# manifests/ directory may hold a registry pull secret, so the whole tree is
# ignored rather than matched by pattern: nothing under this directory is
# committed except this file.
#
# The chart, in ../helm/charts/helix-web, is where the shape of a deployment
# lives, with every option documented in its values.yaml; these files only
# fill it in. For a shareable starting point, see ../README.md rather than
# un-ignoring one of these.
*
!.gitignore
